---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../config/site";
import { breadcrumbs } from "../data/jsonld";
import { PERMISSIONS } from "../data/permissions";
const desc = "Showsteps stores everything on your device, has no account and no analytics, and makes no network requests after install. Every permission explained.";
---
<Base title="Privacy" description={desc} path="/privacy/" jsonLd={[breadcrumbs([{ name: "Showsteps", path: "/" }, { name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy/" }])]}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Nothing leaves your browser</h1>
      <p class="lede">Short version: Showsteps has no server, no account and no analytics. What you record stays on your computer until you export a file yourself.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What Showsteps stores, and where</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Guides, step text and screenshots are stored in your browser's IndexedDB on your computer.</li>
          <li>Your settings (for example the highlight colour and which kinds of data to mask) are stored in the extension's local storage. While a recording runs, its state is kept in Chrome's session storage, which lives in memory and is cleared when the browser closes, so a recording survives Chrome suspending the extension's background worker.</li>
          <li>Exports are files you save. Showsteps does not track where you send them.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>What leaves your computer</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing. The extension makes no network requests after install: no analytics, no crash reporting, no update pings of its own
          (Chrome updates extensions itself), and no AI service. When you press a support link, your browser opens this website in a
          normal tab; that is separate from the extension.
        </p>
        <h2>Passwords and sensitive fields</h2>
        <p>
          While you record, Showsteps looks for password fields and for card numbers, tax IDs, IBANs, API keys and tokens, both in form
          fields and in text on the page. The typed value is not saved, and what was found is masked before the screenshot is stored, so
          the original never reaches the guide. Numbers that only look similar, such as order numbers and timestamps, are left alone.
          Auto-detection is a safety net, not a guarantee: it cannot know that a name in a table is a real customer. Review every
          screenshot before sharing, and use the blur and crop tools.
        </p>
        <h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
        <p>
          These are the sentences we give Chrome Web Store reviewers for each permission, word for word. Showsteps asks for nothing else:
          no <code>tabs</code>, <code>webNavigation</code>, <code>downloads</code>, <code>webRequest</code> or <code>cookies</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Permissions" tabindex="0">
          <table class="compare">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Permission</th><th scope="col">Why Showsteps needs it</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {PERMISSIONS.map((p) => (
                <tr><th scope="row">{p.code ? <code>{p.name}</code> : p.name}</th><td>{p.why}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <h2 id="check">Check it yourself: no network</h2>
        <p>
          You do not have to take our word for it. Chrome will show you every request the extension makes. It takes about five minutes.
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Open <code>chrome://extensions</code> and switch on Developer mode (top right).</li>
          <li>Find Showsteps and click <strong>service worker</strong> next to <em>Inspect views</em>. DevTools opens for the extension&rsquo;s background worker.</li>
          <li>Open the <strong>Network</strong> tab and leave the window open. Keep <em>Preserve log</em> ticked.</li>
          <li>Record a short task on any page, using made-up data, then stop, edit a step and export a file.</li>
          <li>Look at the list. It should hold no requests to any domain. Do the same in the side panel or editor: right-click inside it, choose <strong>Inspect</strong>, and watch its Network tab.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          For a check that covers the whole browser, open <code>chrome://net-export</code>, start logging, do the same recording, stop
          and read the saved log for the extension&rsquo;s traffic. To see it work offline, turn Wi-Fi off and repeat the recording;
          nothing should change.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pressing a support link is the one exception, and it is not the extension talking: Chrome opens this website in a normal tab.
        </p>
        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          The site you are reading has no analytics, no cookies and no third-party requests. Its fonts are served from the same origin.
        </p>
        <h2>Payments</h2>
        <p>
          Support payments are handled by Stripe on Stripe's own pages. Showsteps never sees your card details, and the extension does not
          know whether you have given.
        </p>
        <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
        <p>
          The source is on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>, so any change to this behaviour is visible in the history. Questions can go
          to the <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>issue tracker</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
